s to. A value of 1 is assumed if not present.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"isAdditional","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this clef is in a non-standard line position, such as for a cue passage or when multiple clefs are present on one staff simultaneously.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"size","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The size of the clef, used when ","type":"text"},{"code":"additional","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", typically to indicate cue clefs.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"isAfterBarline","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this clef appears after the barline rather than before it, as for cues or after a repeated section.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"printsObject","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest). Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoic